  {
   "n": 1,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "single | Marks +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Two infinite line charges, each having linear charge density +5 &mu;C/m, are placed parallel to the&nbsp;z-axis at (2,0) m and (-2,0) m. The magnitude of the electric field at the origin is:</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>22.5 &times; 10<sup>3</sup> V/m</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>45 &times; 10<sup>3</sup> V/m</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>90 &times; 10<sup>3</sup> V/m</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>0</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>The fields due to the two identical positive line charges at the origin are equal in magnitude and&nbsp;opposite in direction.<br>Therefore, E<sub>net</sub> = 0</p>"
  },
